# Story: As a security officer, I want repeated failed sign-ins to lock an account for a while, so that passwords cannot be guessed by trying many of them. After five failed sign-ins for one username within fifteen minutes, sign-in for that username is refused for five minutes with TOO_MANY_ATTEMPTS, even with the right password. Other accounts are not affected.

@draft
Feature: Account Lockout After Multiple Failed Login Attempts

  Scenario Outline: User account is locked after five failed login attempts within fifteen minutes
    Given a user with username "<username>"
    When the user tries to log in with wrong password "<wrong_password>" {int} times within "15" minutes
    Then the user receives TOO_MANY_ATTEMPTS error message

    Examples:
      | username  | wrong_password |
      | alice     | secret         |

  Scenario: User can log in after account unlock period
    Given a user with username "<username>"
    When the user tries to log in with wrong password "<wrong_password>" five times within "15" minutes
    Then the user receives TOO_MANY_ATTEMPTS error message
    And the user waits for "5" minutes
    When the user logs in with correct password "<correct_password>"
    Then the login is successful

  Scenario: User cannot log in during lockout period even with correct credentials
    Given a user with username "<username>" and correct password "<correct_password>"
    When the user tries to log in with wrong password "<wrong_password>" five times within "15" minutes
    Then the user receives TOO_MANY_ATTEMPTS error message
    And the user attempts to log in with correct password "<correct_password>"
    Then the login is refused because TOO_MANY_ATTEMPTS

  Scenario: Other users are not affected by another's account lockout
    Given a user with username "<username>" and correct password "<correct_password>"
    When the user tries to log in with wrong password "<wrong_password>" five times within "15" minutes
    Then the user receives TOO_MANY_ATTEMPTS error message
    And another user with different username "<other_username>" logs in with their correct password "<other_correct_password>"
    Then the login is successful

  Scenario: Account lockout resets after waiting period
    Given a user with username "<username>"
    When the user tries to log in with wrong password "<wrong_password>" five times within "15" minutes
    Then the user receives TOO_MANY_ATTEMPTS error message
    And the user waits for "6" minutes
    When the user logs in with correct password "<correct_password>"
    Then the login is successful

  Scenario: Account lockout does not affect other users' logins
    Given a user with username "<username>" and another user with different username "<other_username>"
    When the first user tries to log in with wrong password "<wrong_password>" five times within "15" minutes
    Then the first user receives TOO_MANY_ATTEMPTS error message
    And the second user logs in with their correct password "<other_correct_password>"
    Then the login is successful

  Scenario: Account lockout does not prevent other users from logging in after waiting period
    Given a user with username "<username>" and another user with different username "<other_username>"
    When the first user tries to log in with wrong password "<wrong_password>" five times within "15" minutes
    Then the first user receives TOO_MANY_ATTEMPTS error message
    And the second user waits for "6" minutes
    When the second user logs in with their correct password "<other_correct_password>"
    Then the login is successful
